# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in. Never commit the real key.
# Only the local server reads this file; secrets are never sent to the browser.

# Which AI to start with: "claude" (paid, best quality, default), "gemini" or "groq" (free tiers), or "ollama"
# (free, local). You can change it per task in the app (AI setup); a provider only appears there when its key is set.
# AI_PROVIDER=claude

# --- Claude (AI_PROVIDER=claude) ---
# Your CV text (without name/contact details) and the job advert are sent to Anthropic's API.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional: model (default claude-opus-5-5; claude-haiku-5-5 is much cheaper) and timeout per call in ms
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=
# AI_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# --- Ollama (AI_PROVIDER=ollama) --- free, and everything stays on this computer
# 1. Install from https://ollama.com   2. ollama pull llama3.1   3. set AI_PROVIDER=ollama and restart
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.1
# OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434   (must be this machine)
# OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=16384   (context size; the CV and the prompt need a lot)
# Local models on a CPU can take minutes. AI_TIMEOUT_MS defaults to 15 minutes for Ollama; a smaller model
# (for example llama3.2:3b) is much faster.

# --- Gemini (AI_PROVIDER=gemini) --- Google, free tier
# The masked CV text and the job advert go to Google. FREE TIERS MAY USE WHAT YOU SEND TO IMPROVE THE MODELS:
# do not use this for anything sensitive (use Ollama). Names and contact details are masked, but employer names,
# dates and wording can still identify you.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# --- Groq (AI_PROVIDER=groq) --- free tier
# Same caution as Gemini: check Groq's data terms; use Ollama for anything sensitive.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# Groq changes which models a key can use (Llama ones marked "Contact Sales" give a 404).
# Pick a production model from https://console.groq.com/docs/models
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# --- Send feedback (optional) ---
# A GitHub token (fine-grained, only "Issues: write" on the Squeezy CV repository) lets the feedback button create
# issues. Without it the button opens a prefilled GitHub page instead. Only this server reads it.
# FEEDBACK_GITHUB_TOKEN=
